{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS7DZ4no6ctS9T6QUQmF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1647,"cache_read_input_tokens":25579,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1647},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f0e4aa9-7dd1-4a7b-910a-c02f6e0d9208","uuid":"13f6561d-235c-4931-add5-8a866c936dd3","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:26:16.622Z","request_id":"req_011CgS7DYnR84Vgkwh1Q4b7Z","thinking_duration_ms":440,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS7DZ4no6ctS9T6QUQmF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BFMJQLPkXYK74inQnE7Hna","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-tVxobE/ANSWER.md","content":"# HR corridors clamped to the watch's zones — fix\n\n## Cause\n\n`gen.py` built every HR target as `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}`.\nThe readback of event 184233 (`readback/event-184233-as-sent.json`) shows those\nkeys exactly as sent, so the API did not change them. The watch then displayed\neach corridor as one of its own zone bands (118–137, 151–162, …), which matches\na lap-HR / zone-mapped target rather than an instant-HR corridor.\n\n## Change\n\n`gen.py`, `hr_target()`: the lower bound key is now `start` instead of `value`:\n\n```python\nreturn {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}\n```\n\nA docstring explains the choice. Nothing else in the generator changed.\n\nCheck: regenerating `plans/tempo-run.json` now yields `start`/`end` pairs with\nthe planned percentages (68/75, 88/93, 75/82, 65/72) and no `value` keys.\n\n## Which parts of the colleague's note applied\n\n- **Applied: `start` instead of `value` for the corridor's lower bound, with\n  `%lthr` percentages.** Our readback points to the same problem (zone-clamped\n  display with `value`/`end`), and the note's shape matches our intent of\n  percentages converted by Intervals from its stored LTHR.\n- **Not applied: a top-level `description` in Intervals' text grammar.** Our\n  readback shows `workout_doc.steps` populated, so the parser already accepts\n  the event. The note's description trick is for web-UI step rendering, which is\n  not the reported problem. Adding it would be a separate change.\n- **Not applied: the `m` / `mtr` / `Z<n>` / label-digit rules.** They only\n  matter for the `description` text, which we do not send.\n- **Not applied: the \"Instant HR\" UI round-trip.** That was the colleague's\n  route to the key name. Here, the `start` key comes from the note itself.\n\n## Not verified\n\nI could not check the watch or the Intervals export from here, and the ground\nrules bar pushing or reporting anything externally, so I did not run `push.sh`.\nThe `start` routing is the colleague's finding applied to our code, not something\nI observed. To confirm:\n\n1. Regenerate with `python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json > event.json`.\n2. Push with `./push.sh event.json`, then `GET` the event and confirm `start`\n   is kept.\n3. Sync through Garmin Connect and check that the Tempo step shows about\n   151–160 bpm (88–93% × 172), not 151–162 or any zone edge. Float should show\n   about 129–141.\n\nIf the watch still shows zone bands, the next thing to check is whether\nIntervals' export needs the event's type or units changed. Note that the\ncolleague's `start` finding was reported on a different setup, so it may not\ncarry over.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1647,"cache_read_input_tokens":25579,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1647},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f0e4aa9-7dd1-4a7b-910a-c02f6e0d9208","uuid":"15c0d41b-f99b-4e5e-b75c-097715280222","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:26:21.029Z","request_id":"req_011CgS7DYnR84Vgkwh1Q4b7Z","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01BFMJQLPkXYK74inQnE7Hna":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-tVxobE/ANSWER.md","content":"# HR corridors clamped to the watch's zones — fix\n\n## Cause\n\n`gen.py` built every HR target as `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}`.\nThe readback of event 184233 (`readback/event-184233-as-sent.json`) shows those\nkeys exactly as sent, so the API did not change them. The watch then displayed\neach corridor as one of its own zone bands (118–137, 151–162, …), which matches\na lap-HR / zone-mapped target rather than an instant-HR corridor.\n\n## Change\n\n`gen.py`, `hr_target()`: the lower bound key is now `start` instead of `value`:\n\n```python\nreturn {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}\n```\n\nA docstring explains the choice. Nothing else in the generator changed.\n\nCheck: regenerating `plans/tempo-run.json` now yields `start`/`end` pairs with\nthe planned percentages (68/75, 88/93, 75/82, 65/72) and no `value` keys.\n\n## Which parts of the colleague's note applied\n\n- **Applied: `start` instead of `value` for the corridor's lower bound, with\n  `%lthr` percentages.** Our readback points to the same problem (zone-clamped\n  display with `value`/`end`), and the note's shape matches our intent of\n  percentages converted by Intervals from its stored LTHR.\n- **Not applied: a top-level `description` in Intervals' text grammar.** Our\n  readback shows `workout_doc.steps` populated, so the parser already accepts\n  the event. The note's description trick is for web-UI step rendering, which is\n  not the reported problem. Adding it would be a separate change.\n- **Not applied: the `m` / `mtr` / `Z<n>` / label-digit rules.** They only\n  matter for the `description` text, which we do not send.\n- **Not applied: the \"Instant HR\" UI round-trip.** That was the colleague's\n  route to the key name. Here, the `start` key comes from the note itself.\n\n## Not verified\n\nI could not check the watch or the Intervals export from here, and the ground\nrules bar pushing or reporting anything externally, so I did not run `push.sh`.\nThe `start` routing is the colleague's finding applied to our code, not something\nI observed. To confirm:\n\n1. Regenerate with `python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json > event.json`.\n2. Push with `./push.sh event.json`, then `GET` the event and confirm `start`\n   is kept.\n3. Sync through Garmin Connect and check that the Tempo step shows about\n   151–160 bpm (88–93% × 172), not 151–162 or any zone edge. Float should show\n   about 129–141.\n\nIf the watch still shows zone bands, the next thing to check is whether\nIntervals' export needs the event's type or units changed. Note that the\ncolleague's `start` finding was reported on a different setup, so it may not\ncarry over.\n"}}}
