ing it would be a separate change.\n- **Not applied: the `m` / `mtr` / `Z<n>` / label-digit rules.** They only\n  matter for the `description` text, which we do not send.\n- **Not applied: the \"Instant HR\" UI round-trip.** That was the colleague's\n  route to the key name. Here, the `start` key comes from the note itself.\n\n## Not verified\n\nI could not check the watch or the Intervals export from here, and the ground\nrules bar pushing or reporting anything externally, so I did not run `push.sh`.\nThe `start` routing is the colleague's finding applied to our code, not something\nI observed. To confirm:\n\n1. Regenerate with `python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json > event.json`.\n2. Push with `./push.sh event.json`, then `GET` the event and confirm `start`\n   is kept.\n3. Sync through Garmin Connect and check that the Tempo step shows about\n   151–160 bpm (88–93% × 172), not 151–162 or any zone edge. Float should show\n   about 129–141.\n\nIf the watch still shows zone bands, the next thing to check is whether\nIntervals' export needs the event's type or units changed. Note that the\ncolleague's `start` finding was reported on a different setup, so it may not\ncarry over.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BFMJQLPkXYK74inQnE7Hna","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS7DzQ2zDWzS5N3Rdwa4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I changed the generator so HR corridors use `start` instead of `value` as the lower bound. I have not verified the fix on the watch, because I didn't push anything.\n\n**Cause:** `gen.py` built each HR target as `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}`. The readback of event 184233 shows those keys going out unchanged, and the watch displayed each corridor as one of its own zone bands. That matches the colleague's note: `value`/`end` routes to a zone-mapped target.\n\n**Change:** `hr_target()` in `gen.py` now returns `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}`, with a docstring explaining why. I regenerated the Tempo run plan to a temp file. It now has start/end pairs of 68/75, 88/93, 75/82 and 65/72, and no `value` keys.\n\n**From the colleague's note:**\n- **Applied:** the `start` key for the lower bound, with `%lthr` percentages.\n- **Not applied:** the top-level `description` text. Our readback already shows `workout_doc.steps` populated, so the parser accepts the event, and the description only affects web-UI rendering.\n- **Not applied:** the description grammar rules and the \"Instant HR\" UI round-trip, since they only matter for that description or for finding the key name.\n\n**Not verified:** I didn't run `push.sh`, since the ground rules bar submitting anything externally. The `start` behaviour is the colleague's finding applied here, not something I observed. To confirm, push the regenerated event, check the API keeps `start`, sync through Garmin Connect, and check that the Tempo step shows about 151–160 bpm. If it still shows zone bands, the next check is the event's type or units.\n\nThe changes are uncommitted. `ANSWER.md` at the repo root has the full write-up and the verification steps."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"